WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. From its ranch and farmland outskirts, to its humble, close-knit community of several thousand residents, the township of Cisco is emblematic of traditional rural Texas. Its quaint character hasn't changed much over the decades, except briefly during the 1920s, when the population more than tripled to nearly 8,000 people.
我们的节目涉及严肃且往往令人痛苦的事件。如果您在任何时候感到需要支持，请联系您当地的危机中心。有关机密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您使用的应用上或我们网站上的本期节目简介。思科镇从其牧场和田园边缘，到其拥有数千名居民的简朴紧密社区，是传统德克萨斯州乡村的象征。几十年来，它古雅的特色并没有太大变化，只是在20世纪20年代短暂地经历过一次变化，当时人口激增了两倍多，达到了近8,000人。

2
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:33.000
At the time, Cisco was nested on the edge of one of the United States' most productive oil fields, prompting an influx of newcomers hoping to make a fortune from the black gold, or Texas tea as it was known. The oil boom brought prosperity to Cisco and its residents, and the town soon boasted a city charter and a new railroad. Although the height of the boom had passed by the late 1920s, by which point many had obtained the riches they sought, others continued to find new and innovative ways to keep making money.
当时，思科坐落在美国最富饶的油田之一的边缘，吸引了大批新来者，他们希望能从这些黑金（当时被称为德克萨斯茶）中发财。石油繁荣为思科及其居民带来了繁荣，这座城镇很快就拥有了城市特许状和一条新铁路。尽管到20世纪20年代末，石油繁荣的高峰已经过去，当时许多人已经获得了他们追求的财富，但其他人仍在继续寻找新的创新方式来赚钱。

3
00:01:33.000 --> 00:02:16.000
It was the era of prohibition, but in Texas, opponents of the alcohol ban were in control of the government and refused to enforce its policies. The South became a major producer and distributor of illicit whiskey, better known as Moonshine, and bootlegging was favorably tolerated. At the heart of Cisco's business center was a wide paved boulevard lined with sturdy red brick architecture that housed typical small-town fare, a post office, hotel, antique stores, and a bank. In December 1927, the boulevard sparkled in green, red, and gold for Christmas.
那是禁酒令时期，但在德克萨斯州，反对禁酒令的人控制了政府，并拒绝执行其政策。南方成为非法威士忌（更为人所知的名字是私酿酒）的主要生产和分销地，走私酒受到了宽容对待。思科商业中心的中心是一条宽阔的铺面大道，两旁是坚固的红砖建筑，里面有典型的小镇设施，包括邮局、酒店、古董店和银行。1927年12月，这条大道为圣诞节闪烁着绿、红、金三色光芒。

4
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:51.000
Creative decor was prominently displayed in storefronts, and the streets were filled with children who had been released from school for the holiday break. On Friday, December 23, two days before Christmas, Cisco's children were alerted to a very special arrival in town. Santa Claus in his red suit, silvery hair, and matching curly beard was making his way down the main street. Children mobbed the beloved character, while some adults noted this Santa was significantly thinner than usual.
创意装饰在店面显眼处展示，街上挤满了因学校放圣诞假而出来玩的孩子们。12月23日星期五，圣诞节前两天，思科的孩子们接到通知，镇上将迎来一位非常特殊的访客。穿着红衣服、有着银色头发和相配的卷曲胡须的圣诞老人正沿着主街走来。孩子们蜂拥而上围住这个深受喜爱的角色，而一些成年人则注意到这个圣诞老人明显比平时瘦。

5
00:02:51.000 --> 00:03:27.000
His trademark red robe looked cheap, it was clearly homemade, and barely covered his street clothes underneath. He carried neither sweets to give the children, nor a collection tin for charity. Instead, he held an empty brown burlap sack with Idaho potatoes stenciled across the front. Santa paused before a young boy and shook his hand, asking, Well, little man, what do you want for Christmas? The boy wanted to become a football player when he grew up, and requested a football from a store across the road.
他标志性的红袍看起来很廉价，显然是自制的，几乎盖不住里面穿的街头服装。他既没有带给孩子们的糖果，也没有带用于慈善的募捐罐。相反，他拿着一个空的棕色麻布袋，袋子正面印有爱达荷土豆的字样。圣诞老人停在一个小男孩面前，和他握手，问道：“好吧，小家伙，你圣诞节想要什么？”男孩长大后想成为一名足球运动员，并要求得到路对面一家商店的一个足球。

6
00:03:27.000 --> 00:04:01.000
He grabbed Santa's hand and tried to drag him towards the shop, but Santa shook him off, explaining he couldn't deviate from his path. He told the boy to point the gift out to his parents, and that Father Christmas would surely leave it under the tree for him. Santa hastened his steps, but couldn't shake the crowd of children that was now following him. Some expressed their disappointment that he wasn't handing out candy or small gifts, while the older children declared that he wasn't the real Santa at all.
他抓住圣诞老人的手，试图把他拉向商店，但圣诞老人甩开了他，解释说他不能偏离路线。他告诉男孩把礼物指给父母看，圣诞老人肯定会把它留在树下。圣诞老人加快了脚步，但还是甩不掉现在正跟着他的一群孩子。有些人对没有分发糖果或小礼物表示失望，而稍大一点的孩子则宣称他根本不是真正的圣诞老人。

7
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:41.000
As he entered the front door of the first National Bank of Cisco, which sat on the corner of Main Street and a narrow alleyway, the grown-ups chuckled that even Saint Nick had a banking business to tend to during the holiday season. When the bell over the bank's door rang, cashier Alec Spears looked up from tending to a customer and called out a cheery, Hello Santa? Without a word, the man in the red suit made his way to the desk in the middle of the lobby, ignoring the children still following behind. Thinking perhaps Saint Nick hadn't heard him, Alec's kept up the Christmas cheer with
当他走进位于主街和一条狭窄小巷拐角处的思科第一国民银行前门时，大人们笑着说，连圣尼古拉在假期里也有银行业务要处理。当银行门上的铃铛响起时，出纳员亚历克·斯皮尔斯（Alec Spears）从照顾客户中抬起头，欢快地喊道：“你好，圣诞老人？”那个穿红衣服的人一言不发，径直走向大厅中央的桌子，无视后面仍然跟着的孩子们。亚历克以为圣尼古拉可能没听到他，于是继续保持着圣诞节的欢乐气氛

8
00:04:41.000 --> 00:05:51.000
another call of, Hello Santa Claus? Again, there was no response from Saint Nick. The other bank patrons were paying such close attention to him that they barely noticed when the bell above the door rang out again as three men entered. The trio quietly drew pistols out from beneath their bulky coats and yelled, Stick em up, this is a robbery. In the United States, the 1920s had been deemed the golden age of crime. By 1926, many parts of Texas showed the early signs of entering into a depression, and desperation
又喊了一声：“你好，圣诞老人？”圣尼古拉依然没有任何回应。其他银行顾客对他的关注如此之高，以至于当门上的铃铛再次响起，三名男子走进来时，他们几乎没有注意到。这三名男子悄悄地从臃肿的外套下掏出手枪，大喊道：“举起手来，这是抢劫。”在美国，20世纪20年代被誉为犯罪的黄金时代。到1926年，德克萨斯州的许多地区显示出进入萧条期的早期迹象，绝望情绪

9
00:05:51.000 --> 00:06:36.000
from those who had lost everything caused the rapid increase in the number of bank robberies. Between 1920 and 1929, insurance companies reported that property crime from bank robberies to drugstore holdups increased by 1700%. Banks in rural areas were particularly vulnerable. When robberies grew to a frequency of three to four per week, the Texas Bankers Association established the popular, yet controversial, dead bank robber reward program. As part of the scheme, anyone who shot and killed a robber during the act of holding up a bank was rewarded with $5,000 cash, no questions asked.
来自失去一切的人导致银行抢劫案数量急剧增加。在1920年至1929年期间，保险公司报告称，从银行抢劫到药店抢劫的财产犯罪增加了1700%。农村地区的银行尤其脆弱。当抢劫频率增加到每周三到四次时，德克萨斯州银行家协会设立了广受欢迎却又备受争议的“击毙银行劫匪悬赏计划”。作为该计划的一部分，任何人在抢劫银行的过程中开枪打死劫匪，都将获得5,000美元现金奖励，无需多问。

10
00:06:36.000 --> 00:07:24.000
The bounty would not be paid in the event the robber was merely injured. The program garnered considerable media attention, and while some viewed it as an extreme measure, many celebrated it as an effective remedy where the culprits got what they deserved. Justice Ben Lindsay, a progressive judge and social reformer based in Denver, Colorado, was firmly against the dead bank robber reward program, and stated, I am amazed that such a conservative group in Texas as the bankers would lend themselves to a practice that is so fraught with consequences to the orderly processes of justice. The danger lies in the possibility that some grotesque mockery of justice may result,
如果劫匪仅受伤，则不予支付赏金。该计划获得了相当大的媒体关注，虽然有些人认为这是一项极端措施，但许多人将其庆祝为一种有效的救济手段，让罪犯得到了应有的下场。本·林德西（Ben Lindsay）法官是科罗拉多州丹佛市的一位进步派法官和社会改革家，他坚决反对击毙银行劫匪悬赏计划，并表示：“我很惊讶，德克萨斯州的银行家这样一个保守的群体，竟然会参与一种对有序的司法进程带来如此严重后果的做法。危险在于可能会产生某种对正义的怪诞嘲弄，”

11
00:07:24.000 --> 00:08:17.000
especially if some peace officer in his zeal to collect $5,000 should shoot down an innocent man. I see no reason why the bankers should set themselves up as Lord High executioners. Justice Justice Lindsay predicted that wasn't long until flaws in the system began to emerge. Few robbers were killed during banking hours or in the actual commission of a robbery. Instead, most of the shootings occurred at night and under suspicious circumstances. Many were carried out by local police officers who arrived at the scene after receiving alleged tip-offs. In one incident, four Mexican laborers were picked up by two men, including a deputy sheriff, under the pretense of offering them work.
“特别是如果某个治安官为了收集5,000美元而热心地枪杀了一个无辜的人。我看不出银行家有什么理由把自己打扮成大法官。”林德西法官预测，该系统的漏洞开始显现只是时间问题。在银行营业时间内或在实际抢劫过程中被杀的劫匪很少。相反，大多数枪击事件发生在夜间且情况可疑的情况下。许多枪击事件是由当地警察实施的，他们在接到所谓的举报后赶到现场。在起事件中，两名男子（包括一名副警长）以提供工作为借口，带走了四名墨西哥劳工。

12
00:08:17.000 --> 00:09:09.000
The workers were driven to a rural town and were told to wait by the local bank branch. Shortly afterwards, the church across the street mysteriously caught fire, capturing the attention of the town's folk. In the ensuing panic, the deputy and his friend rushed upon the four Mexican workers and started shooting, killing two and seriously wounding a third. The two gunmen alleged that the workers were preparing to rob the bank. The surviving victims testified that the entire scenario was a setup, concocted by the deputy and his friend to collect the $5,000 banked rubber bounty. They were prosecuted for the crime, but there were many more thwarted robberies where the bandits did not live to dispute the shooter's version of events.
这些工人被驱车带到一个乡村小镇，并被告知在当地银行分行旁等候。不久之后，街对面的教堂神秘起火，吸引了镇上居民的注意力。在随后的混乱中，副警长和他的朋友冲向四名墨西哥工人并开始开枪，打死两人，重伤第三人。两名枪手声称这些工人正准备抢劫银行。幸存的受害者作证说，整个场景是一个圈套，由副警长和他的朋友精心策划，以收集5,000美元的击毙银行劫匪赏金。他们因罪行而被起诉，但还有更多被挫败的抢劫案，劫匪没有活下来去反驳枪手对事件的说法。

13
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:57.000
Since the introduction of the rewards program, losses faced by the banks had decreased significantly, even after factoring in the bounty payments. As such, the Texas Bankers Association refused to withdraw the program, but an amendment was made to the policy wording to clarify the reward was only available in the case of lawful shootings, which occurred in daylight during the actual commission of a robbery. Shortly before the man in the Santa Claus suit walked into Cisco's first national bank, he caught the attention of six-year-old Francis Blasingame. The child begged her mother to take her to meet him, and though Mrs. Blasingame was reluctant,
自悬赏计划推出以来，银行面临的损失显着减少，即使在计入赏金支出之后也是如此。因此，德克萨斯州银行家协会拒绝撤销该计划，但对政策措辞进行了修改，以澄清悬赏仅适用于在白天实际抢劫过程中发生的合法枪击事件。就在身穿圣诞老人服装的男子走进思科第一国民银行之前，他吸引了六岁的弗朗西丝·布拉辛盖姆（Francis Blasingame）的注意。小女孩乞求母亲带她去见他，尽管布拉辛盖姆夫人有些不情愿，

14
