and formed an impromptu posse. Jumping into vehicles and on horseback, they started in pursuit of the Buick, initiating the largest manhunt in the history of Texas. Several of the robbers were nursing injuries and one was bleeding profusely all over the Buick's plush gray upholstery. The group yelled at one another as their two young hostages remained silent. Of the pair, Laverne Coma had reason to be especially fearful. She had visited the bank that day hoping to withdraw some of her hard-earned money to buy Christmas presents for her family, and although he was still wearing his scrappy disguise, she had recognized Santa. Laverne's mother had bought a cafe from his mother a year prior, and he still dined at the establishment
并组建了一支临时搜捕队。他们跳上汽车和马背，开始追捕别克车，拉开了德克萨斯州历史上最大规模搜捕行动的序幕。几名劫匪受了伤，其中一人在别克车毛绒灰色的内饰上流血不止。这群人互相大喊大叫，而他们两名年轻的人质则保持沉默。在这两人中，拉韦恩·科马有理由感到格外害怕。她那天去银行是希望能取出一些辛苦赚来的钱为家人买圣诞礼物，尽管他身上还穿着破烂的伪装，但她认出了圣诞老人。拉韦恩的母亲一年前从他母亲那里买下了一家咖啡馆，而他至今仍在那家店里用餐

